The pdf skill is authored by the ultrawork project. It is not derived from Anthropic's
proprietary document skills, and the earlier openai/skills `skills/.curated/pdf`
(Apache-2.0) content it replaced was removed in full — SKILL.md, scripts, fixtures and
capabilities.json are written from scratch (see docs/discussions/059 §5 L0 for the
clean-room gate that checks this).

It invokes the following third-party Python libraries at runtime (NOT bundled; installed
by the user per the SKILL.md instructions):
  - pypdfium2 (Apache-2.0 / BSD-3-Clause; wraps PDFium, BSD-3-Clause)
  - pypdf (BSD-3-Clause)
  - pdfplumber (MIT; pulls in pdfminer.six, MIT, and Pillow, MIT-CMU)
  - reportlab (BSD-3-Clause)

This skill was originally built on PyMuPDF and has been moved off it in full. PyMuPDF is
AGPL-3.0-or-commercial, and its rightsholder (Artifex, also the Ghostscript rightsholder,
cf. Artifex v. Hancom) enforces that licence — a commercially distributed product cannot
carry it without buying one. No file in this skill imports fitz.

Fonts: generated documents embed a CJK face found on the machine doing the generating.
No font is redistributed by this repository.
